<code>assert \old(this.containsKey(key)) => (\result == \old(this.get(key)));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \old(this.containsKey(key)) => (\result == \old(this.get(key)));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \old(this.containsKey(key)) => (\result == \old(this.get(key)));</code>
--------------------
Looking at the comment, it expresses: if a previous mapping existed for the key (i.e., the map contained the key), then the returned value equals the value previously associated with that key.

The relevant observers are `containsKey(key)` for the premise and `get(key)` for the old associated value.

<code>assert \old(this.containsKey(key)) => \result == \old(this.get(key));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \old(this.containsKey(key)) => (\result == \old(this.get(key)));</code>
--------------------
